{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A reproduced long thinking event loses its tail from the owner copy, omitting potentially useful diagnostic text."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After a rollback, an editor can read retained owner diagnostics because the previous release lacks the new read restrictions."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Garbage collection can cause a diagnostic ID to be reused, so an active follow cursor silently misses the new diagnostic."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A reproduced preview build can read owner-only diagnostic text and expose it through a public stage summary."}]}